@coderabbitai Verified against current PR-owned code: there is no existing drift check, but this is an additive guardrail rather than a correctness/security defect in this dependency fix. The current override still installs `remotelyliving/php-dns` 4.3.0 with the intentional `guzzlehttp/promises` `^1.3 || ^2.5` constraint; `composer show ... --locked` confirms `guzzlehttp/promises` 2.5.0.

Recommended follow-up task: add a focused CI/script check comparing the local package override metadata with upstream, allowlisting the intentional promises constraint plus expected `source`/`dist`/`version` differences. Keeping that outside this bounded PR scope.

